BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 736 Tm (Because floating-point arithmetic can produce precision problems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 722 Tm (Integer cents are safer for financial calculations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 700 Tm (Why use a service layer?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 677 Tm (Because role logic, summary logic, and data visibility rules do not belong in raw SQL or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 663 Tm (routing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 649 Tm (The service layer is where business logic should live.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 627 Tm (Why use repositories?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 604 Tm (Because SQL should be centralized.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 590 Tm (If I later move from SQLite to PostgreSQL or SQLAlchemy, the impact is isolated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 568 Tm (Why simplified authentication?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 545 Tm (The assignment explicitly allowed simple assumptions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 531 Tm (So I used `X-User-Id` to keep focus on backend design and access logic.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 509 Tm (Why seed data?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 486 Tm (It improves reviewer experience and makes demos fast.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 464 Tm (Interview Questions And Strong Answers) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 438 Tm (Q. How does a transaction creation request work end to end?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 415 Tm (Answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 401 Tm ("The API route parses the JSON body and forwards it to the service layer. The service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 387 Tm (validates the payload, checks that the caller is an admin, confirms the target user) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 373 Tm (exists, and then calls the repository to insert the row. After insertion, the repository) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 359 Tm (fetches the created record and the service serializes it into an API-friendly response.") Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 337 Tm (Q. Where is authorization enforced?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 314 Tm (Answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 300 Tm ("Mainly in the service layer. I use a small `require_roles` helper for role checks, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 286 Tm (I also use helper methods like `_target_user_id` and `_assert_transaction_visibility` to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 272 Tm (enforce ownership rules.") Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 250 Tm (Q. How did you avoid repeating validation logic?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 227 Tm (Answer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 213 Tm ("I centralized validation in `models.py` so both create and update flows reuse the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 199 Tm (normalization functions for dates, money, roles, text length, and integer parsing.") Tj ET
